# L §4.6 Reading at a date: "An item keyed by one time index, read with a date or a period of another granularity
# in that key position (cpi[d] for a day d ...), reads the key whose period holds it. A date outside the index is
# RUN-KEY. A period longer than the index's keys holds no key: it is refused (LOAD-KEY)."
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input cpi[m in months]: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  cpi[2026-03] = 101.5

ask q1: cpi[2026-03-17]
ask q2: cpi[2027-01-05]
=== expect
q1: 101.5
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: refused: RUN-KEY ...
  cut 2026-12-31
